{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","created_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_01711f2fdead377bf7f04a760325929316bac472befa423baa88aeb7f32cdd55","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"cpoile/claudemacs@1f2fe7bbc718 snapshot 21761bc18dec649d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_30f9cba236d38f79475cbb35072807847570cb0c4f07d5c53e0f89ecdb15b97f"],"source_ids":["src_032a7bdd99d2580f8a51b80fe281bdd0"],"text":"The project's stated design philosophy is simplicity: let the LLM CLI run in the terminal without agents, MCP, or IDE integration, which the README says would consume context.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","updated_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","created_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_07e61166e02e006eadadc263d7c6305e22ece1bf8f8f7fdcdfe5b5e829e6a2ae","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"cpoile/claudemacs@1f2fe7bbc718 snapshot 21761bc18dec649d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_87bdbc20011bf12d50152fb6731197ee96234f3c9374db1b74e988f05eaa6da5","slc_9fa36a6acccb5510a60bbdca67fd3accb67c209c63ad0e9d9bebdfa4e26d443c","slc_aefa82698a4a77cc3bcd607c1c6ff3cb2107b6f0674ef69d3173853bc2722585"],"source_ids":["src_032a7bdd99d2580f8a51b80fe281bdd0"],"text":"Claudemacs exposes a transient menu (default binding C-c C-e) with core commands for starting, switching, resuming, listing, and killing sessions, plus action commands like fix-error-at-point and implement-comment.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","updated_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","created_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_080b1f5f453171e29b63660d69c9c2b98eac18068d0d64efb1997af9fc23a615","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"cpoile/claudemacs@1f2fe7bbc718 snapshot 21761bc18dec649d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ec5c982a288212511eee7324609a72ddd1c0adbb36c62864c25272d99924c59a"],"source_ids":["src_032a7bdd99d2580f8a51b80fe281bdd0"],"text":"On macOS, clicking a system notification does not bring focus to Emacs; the README notes this limitation and solicits ideas.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","updated_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","created_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_15693131a7e4d2c461a0dfc2e15659b09d4156fc9b7600418f116d630900337e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"cpoile/claudemacs@1f2fe7bbc718 snapshot 21761bc18dec649d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_7f5313c37dd03fabde0e33222d499c83e4cc9da4fdd59a1b299e6566ded71f11","slc_c71303c5784e250948da015ff40ba5fc497d0d0ca67100738b5cc097751976a2","slc_ff8818180eea57cbf2e7d07f93751de801d96f3880e3acf9bbcf9144f3979284"],"source_ids":["src_032a7bdd99d2580f8a51b80fe281bdd0"],"text":"When claudemacs-prefer-projectile-root is set, the tool's cwd uses the projectile root instead of the git root, letting Claude Code read and edit files across sibling repos in a monorepo layout.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","updated_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","created_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_29bf2d6f0a45f0496ae3846729452abbd53f7c85d24ad6462aa6ea8c105b09bb","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"cpoile/claudemacs@1f2fe7bbc718 snapshot 21761bc18dec649d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2c2fb56d150e10c3560e78b28a88dedbbdc8981122e5d528ef5a4bb3584d3c63"],"source_ids":["src_032a7bdd99d2580f8a51b80fe281bdd0"],"text":"Sessions are workspace-aware: the session is keyed to the Doom/Perspective workspace and the tool's cwd defaults to the project's git root, enabling separate sessions per workspace in a monorepo.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","updated_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","created_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_476905049b6a57a6236546ea54f59ae288eb7f728f565a11f16cd31222c7455c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"cpoile/claudemacs@1f2fe7bbc718 snapshot 21761bc18dec649d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_03a2b3cd71cbb0ee7c136d98e3969bbe443a59a6098af78dde184c68f0ab60d4","slc_2e8cd7f0fe90e7380613093acfbe1fd8680114a1c65869a0aecc7d01dd7439fa","slc_813b598f459f70733774b41447232e8c9e63d37deedaaa1b492baedfa145f4f9"],"source_ids":["src_032a7bdd99d2580f8a51b80fe281bdd0"],"text":"A configurable tool registry defines which AI CLI tools are available, with defaults Claude, Codex, and Gemini, each with program, switches, and model-types entries; users can add tools like aider.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","updated_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","created_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_6f3aa1b01844e56b2fd31d8c038278c02b27a5a7e84044fbe2df1af11a8a6de9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"cpoile/claudemacs@1f2fe7bbc718 snapshot 21761bc18dec649d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c81ab18347b65e573cc3d313cb3bbf29927a47c539b7d1ec8d7e4d823afc756d"],"source_ids":["src_032a7bdd99d2580f8a51b80fe281bdd0"],"text":"Claudemacs presents the same session and action commands regardless of which terminal backend is in use.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","updated_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","created_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8e3ac48445948cd819795c05d0f63d7662b5d5602bf1cf47b5a94826ad9aba5d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"cpoile/claudemacs@1f2fe7bbc718 snapshot 21761bc18dec649d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8fc2316bf8bd95ca05e615dd096bee3e040d37872f1a79b99f57e6fb28f03f92","slc_9fa36a6acccb5510a60bbdca67fd3accb67c209c63ad0e9d9bebdfa4e26d443c"],"source_ids":["src_032a7bdd99d2580f8a51b80fe281bdd0"],"text":"Action commands accept a C-u prefix to broadcast the action to all active sessions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","updated_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","created_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9f62331c5650a82ea4704e5594a77d33578039f522966b513d945630bfd83a13","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"cpoile/claudemacs@1f2fe7bbc718 snapshot 21761bc18dec649d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_10383525a74d03576fe14a40fd0737921ecba9407e3d9b8be78f65d7b294d61f"],"source_ids":["src_032a7bdd99d2580f8a51b80fe281bdd0"],"text":"The start-session submenu offers a -d switch to skip permissions (--dangerously-skip-permissions or equivalent) when launching a tool.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","updated_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","created_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_b077a3d34ec28fa2eefdee7350430a793c916292561ef60df558e34894ac0733","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"cpoile/claudemacs@1f2fe7bbc718 snapshot 21761bc18dec649d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_4a386fd81c51d0552560e23f273bc629b8a1eb3b34b4ce0aa99f99166021cc23","slc_4ce299e9d4e70d587a745084009383d44982aa4e593cee71ec490e75306877e9","slc_8fc2316bf8bd95ca05e615dd096bee3e040d37872f1a79b99f57e6fb28f03f92","slc_c81ab18347b65e573cc3d313cb3bbf29927a47c539b7d1ec8d7e4d823afc756d"],"source_ids":["src_032a7bdd99d2580f8a51b80fe281bdd0"],"text":"The package supports multiple terminal backends: Ghostel is selected automatically when available, otherwise it falls back to Eat; the backend can be forced via claudemacs-terminal-backend.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","updated_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","created_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_ba5988dffa1f8669b535e1764a480b9ae58a9b2e912cec2170f99cff33eb0765","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"cpoile/claudemacs@1f2fe7bbc718 snapshot 21761bc18dec649d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_951c883e3d2e517a46941e067b29ccb49fb3d407f19d3d79491dfafc514f1b09"],"source_ids":["src_032a7bdd99d2580f8a51b80fe281bdd0"],"text":"Only the selected terminal backend is loaded; both Eat and Ghostel need not be installed, but the chosen backend must be installed and loadable before starting a session.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","updated_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","created_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_bccf8c3837cb10d79465eaf2b07d0c3a7b7c5e64796e1f26ddb3198d52bcb882","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"cpoile/claudemacs@1f2fe7bbc718 snapshot 21761bc18dec649d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1b2b20a2f7edf38e65a3b260cb3b482d6dad874fe8fdb3f257c815a4b7b788a6","slc_5168fd8d24d4f2c4429baadba41a081b576990dbcb0412e25515d20add0ab403","slc_61be837adfcc9562b0795c373ff6bddf2ea577ffb28c314f83e8038f632ed475","slc_758fb2eaf9a5cf2fee8e8fdb923397cc1b36c70e1534170d100198189e615dc1","slc_8fc2316bf8bd95ca05e615dd096bee3e040d37872f1a79b99f57e6fb28f03f92","slc_cd4cfd4ed39e04bed818e4a3e755964186f696d9734261fc3197a34b5bdc9c81","slc_dbc47cc80cc55e726f3cd12221a9874d85d96967413129deda931f5907276804"],"source_ids":["src_032a7bdd99d2580f8a51b80fe281bdd0"],"text":"System notifications fire (with sound) when the AI tool awaits input or finishes, with per-OS configuration for macOS sounds, Linux notify-send auto-dismiss and canberra sounds, and Windows toast timeouts.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","updated_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","created_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c68efe2d806c40f6837680faeb8cbfba647e1d3092e788004f840a1a392dab44","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"cpoile/claudemacs@1f2fe7bbc718 snapshot 21761bc18dec649d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_39493d65e1c45b415817dc7e0dd2712bf840a9411dde8849ba8326be47b10b4c","slc_bde1fbed7e1b010e717959e75c34b7a7f9da1bdbc90a5b0386a386a0247f438e"],"source_ids":["src_032a7bdd99d2580f8a51b80fe281bdd0"],"text":"The terminal buffer has two interaction modes: a semi-char mode for typing directly to the AI tool and an Emacs mode (C-c C-e) for editing terminal contents, with C-c C-j returning to semi-char mode.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","updated_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","created_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_c7669d6f1cfa1f10a66db4ad5dbdc2fc1f2d37bd46c85894f2b3e73dfd50efa1","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"cpoile/claudemacs@1f2fe7bbc718 snapshot 21761bc18dec649d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_96c91f554d252c4e8d7ec387756f504561d9772cb695b10ac98c08974e6badbf","slc_9b7f7c2a34f86c89eb5a3feee4197c680ec243958181c26877ad59946f8bf5ae"],"source_ids":["src_032a7bdd99d2580f8a51b80fe281bdd0"],"text":"In semi-char mode, C-q acts as a quoted-input escape hatch to send literal control characters (e.g., C-q C-g sends Ctrl-g to Claude Code), while C-g itself is mapped to send ESC.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","updated_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","created_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d5bd91cc7b9707dc6b81263e37d3caf092541479f4f2996098b8a0b300d45509","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"cpoile/claudemacs@1f2fe7bbc718 snapshot 21761bc18dec649d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_89a510106ee81a8679b3227dcdaad6563621ca0cc42f22060721dd7218e6a13f"],"source_ids":["src_032a7bdd99d2580f8a51b80fe281bdd0"],"text":"Requirements are Emacs 28.1+, the Eat package or Ghostel with its native module, transient (built-in since Emacs 28), and a supported AI CLI such as Claude Code.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","updated_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","created_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d5cdf680c0f5c61034e77464009389fae85eb98155a022f0ae08fb1fb328728f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"cpoile/claudemacs@1f2fe7bbc718 snapshot 21761bc18dec649d","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0cb0cfa1c8ef268e964c5d2fe768c8087db1794eb8f8a7b50b8456f19efcc360","slc_b5aa51340607dae9f48cefaf8869cb191d1ab4fcf535c0ed839b76d94a143a43","slc_e95c08788dc943925fe21c52f75612c02defb666fb4750aa706ccd8410a8e401"],"source_ids":["src_032a7bdd99d2580f8a51b80fe281bdd0"],"text":"Terminal-emulator interactions with Claude Code can cause scroll-popping, a stuck input box, or border-drawing issues after window resize; a 'u' unstick command resets the buffer for both backends.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:59Z","updated_by_operation":"op_848f6724ed3746639a84ebea12a28c8a"}
